# Requests for the sample API (Visual Studio, Rider or VS Code's REST Client).
# Start the stack with `docker compose up -d --build`; the API is on port 8080.

@api = http://localhost:8080/api/v1
@consumerB = http://localhost:8082
@apiHost = http://localhost:8080
# GM.Messaging admin endpoints (/admin/messaging) need this header; docker-compose sets the key.
@adminKey = sample-admin-key
@orderId = 3f2c7a10-5b1e-4c8d-9a6f-1e2d3c4b5a60

### Place an order (event: orders.order-placed, ordering key = the order id)
POST {{api}}/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{ "orderId": "{{orderId}}", "customerId": "8d1c2b3a-4e5f-4a6b-9c7d-0e1f2a3b4c5d", "totalAmount": 42.50, "currency": "EUR" }

### Pay it (payments.payment-processed, same ordering key: ConsumerB's timeline gets it after the order)
POST {{api}}/payments
Content-Type: application/json

{ "paymentId": "a1b2c3d4-e5f6-4a7b-8c9d-0e1f2a3b4c5d", "orderId": "{{orderId}}", "amount": 42.50, "status": "Succeeded" }

### Register a user (ConsumerA records it; ConsumerB's inbox worker sends a welcome email)
POST {{api}}/users
Content-Type: application/json

{ "userId": "b2c3d4e5-f6a7-4b8c-9d0e-1f2a3b4c5d6e", "email": "ana@example.test", "name": "Ana" }

### Register a user whose email bounces (ConsumerB's inbox worker retries 3 times, then dead-letters it)
POST {{api}}/users
Content-Type: application/json

{ "userId": "c3d4e5f6-a7b8-4c9d-8e1f-2a3b4c5d6e7f", "email": "nobody@bounce.test", "name": "Bounce" }

### Change stock (inventory.inventory-updated, payload version 2)
POST {{api}}/inventory
Content-Type: application/json

{ "productId": "d4e5f6a7-b8c9-4d0e-9f2a-3b4c5d6e7f80", "warehouse": "TBS-1", "quantityDelta": 5, "newQuantity": 5 }

### An order ConsumerA can't handle (currency XXX): Wolverine retries it, the inbox row records each attempt
POST {{api}}/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{ "orderId": "e5f6a7b8-c9d0-4e1f-8a3b-4c5d6e7f8091", "customerId": "8d1c2b3a-4e5f-4a6b-9c7d-0e1f2a3b4c5d", "totalAmount": 1, "currency": "XXX" }

### Outbox backlog: pending, oldest pending, dead-lettered
GET {{apiHost}}/admin/messaging/outbox
X-Admin-Key: {{adminKey}}

### Dead-lettered outbox messages
GET {{apiHost}}/admin/messaging/outbox/dead-letters
X-Admin-Key: {{adminKey}}

### Requeue one dead-lettered message (after fixing its cause)
POST {{apiHost}}/admin/messaging/outbox/dead-letters/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000/requeue
X-Admin-Key: {{adminKey}}

### Requeue every dead-lettered message
POST {{apiHost}}/admin/messaging/outbox/dead-letters/requeue
X-Admin-Key: {{adminKey}}

### Delete dead-lettered messages older than a date
DELETE {{apiHost}}/admin/messaging/outbox/dead-letters?before=2030-01-01T00:00:00Z
X-Admin-Key: {{adminKey}}

### Readiness: database + outbox backlog
GET http://localhost:8080/health/ready

### ConsumerB's inbox backlog (the inbox worker's pending and dead-lettered rows)
GET {{consumerB}}/admin/messaging/inbox
X-Admin-Key: {{adminKey}}

### ConsumerB's dead-lettered inbox rows (the bounced welcome email)
GET {{consumerB}}/admin/messaging/inbox/dead-letters
X-Admin-Key: {{adminKey}}

### Requeue one dead-lettered inbox row
POST {{consumerB}}/admin/messaging/inbox/dead-letters/consumer-b/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000/requeue
X-Admin-Key: {{adminKey}}

### The broker's dead-letter queue (messages Wolverine gave up on, such as the XXX order)
GET {{consumerB}}/admin/messaging/broker/dead-letters
X-Admin-Key: {{adminKey}}

### Look at them without consuming them
GET {{consumerB}}/admin/messaging/broker/dead-letters/messages
X-Admin-Key: {{adminKey}}

### Replay them to their original queues (after fixing the cause)
POST {{consumerB}}/admin/messaging/broker/dead-letters/replay
X-Admin-Key: {{adminKey}}

### Dry run: count what a replay of ConsumerA's orders would send back, without touching anything
POST {{consumerB}}/admin/messaging/broker/dead-letters/replay?queue=gm.consumer-a.orders&dryRun=true
X-Admin-Key: {{adminKey}}

### Unrouted messages: published to an exchange with no queue bound for them
GET {{consumerB}}/admin/messaging/broker/unrouted
X-Admin-Key: {{adminKey}}

### Move unrouted messages back to their exchange once a queue is bound
POST {{consumerB}}/admin/messaging/broker/unrouted/move?exchange=gm.events
X-Admin-Key: {{adminKey}}

### Every worker's readiness: database, RabbitMQ and its backlog
GET http://localhost:8081/health/ready
